# gts7l: the first-boot wizard's session uses KDE's stock on-screen keyboard.
# The floating keyboard (the users' default) is a normal window, which KWin
# stacks below the fullscreen wizard; the stock one is an input panel, always
# on top. gts7l-setup's helper drops this choice from the kwinrc the new user
# inherits.
#
# Root-owned, like plasma-setup's own entries: its final "Z" line hands the
# whole tree to the plasma-setup user. A plasma-setup-owned .config created
# here made systemd-tmpfiles refuse plasma-setup's root-owned autostart/
# below it ("unsafe path transition"), and the wizard never started.
f /run/plasma-setup/.config/kwinrc 0644 - - - [Wayland]\nInputMethod=/usr/share/applications/org.kde.plasma.keyboard.desktop\n
